    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup centers around capitalizing on the Max Scherzer matchup, where **Bryce Harper** (80.21) remains our premier start. With the wind blowing out and a stellar BvP history against Scherzer, **Harper** is positioned for a high-ceiling performance. We are also leaning heavily into the speed-efficiency profile of **Justin Crawford** (72.83) and the contact prowess of **Luis Arraez** (69.53). Both benefit significantly from the favorable SP_xERA of 5.31 and the aggressive wind conditions, which inflate their respective scores well above their baseline projections. **Jung Hoo Lee** (68.02) rounds out our top-tier offensive cohort; his favorable spot in the two-hole, combined with the platoon advantage against Jobe, makes him a foundational piece for our Roto categories today.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Gavin Sheets** (50.45). While he carries a solid platoon edge against the right-handed Lambert, he ultimately fell short of our efficiency threshold compared to **Masyn Winn** (50.29) and **Tyler Freeman** (50.92). While **Winn** and **Freeman** operate in tougher matchups, their overall utility and roster flexibility necessitated their inclusion over **Sheets**. We are also keeping a watchful eye on **Cal Raleigh** (42.82); his score is suppressed by a difficult matchup against Jax, but his power potential in a 5x5 format keeps him in the lineup despite the proximity to our \"below floor\" cutoff. With **Daulton Varsho** (61.60) and **JJ Bleday** (62.21) offering strong platoon-adjusted value, we are well-positioned to maintain pressure in SB and HR categories, provided we navigate the risks associated with the elite-tier arms lurking in the late innings.",
